        "title": "Menu facelift: gradient area chart, legend chips, stats card",
        "body": "Facelift for the dropdown menu. No behavior changes beyond presentation; all data shown before is still shown (the raw API debug line moved into the stats card tooltip).\n\n## What changed\n\n- vCPU history renders as layered gradient areas (per platform, stacked) with a total line, replacing ~96 skinny bars.\n- Section labels and the peak/avg summaries share one caption style with aligned label/value pairs.\n- Legends are capsule chips; the workflow-run legend only lists statuses that actually occur in the 24h window, so it fits the menu width.\n- The four raw disabled text rows (Active / Queued / API / Updated) are replaced by a stats card: active jobs, active vCPU, queued tiles, per-status history chips, and an updated/sampled footer. Errors render inside the card with a warning tint.\n- The hovered-bucket detail line scales down slightly instead of truncating.\n- Dead code: the old wrapping NSMenuItem text view is removed.\n\n## Before / after\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/BlackBar/7897f006722ea3f82b55f39756ed59c7f221064b/docs/menu-before.png\" width=\"360\"> | <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/BlackBar/7897f006722ea3f82b55f39756ed59c7f221064b/docs/menu-after.png\" width=\"360\"> |\n\nScreenshots taken from the real app against live Blacksmith data (dark mode). All 25 unit tests pass; Codex autoreview clean.\n",
